+### Rarity cards revert to the old banner treatment, on freshly re-supplied evenly-sized art (patch 0364)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Rarity Cards
+- Reverted item cards (gear, potions, Vendor stock, recipe scrolls) from the "Design A" frame art back to the older banner-behind-the-card look
+- The old banner art is now a consistent size across all five rarities, fixing the uneven-sizing issue that was part of why it got replaced in the first place
+- Item icons on these cards are a bit bigger than before
+```
+
+Direct request: patches 0338-0342 shipped and then repeatedly refined "Design A" (the full ornate frame art as the whole card background), but direct feedback after living with it was that the OLDER `.rarity-banner` look (a banner strip behind an otherwise-normal card) actually read better -- its one real problem was that the five `RARITY_BANNER` files were never a consistent size (796x182 up to 957x212, see patch 0324's own writeup on the cropping that caused), which is what originally motivated moving to a full frame image in the first place. Rather than re-fighting that old sizing problem, a freshly-supplied set of all five rarity banners was provided, uniformly 1008x226 this time, dropped straight into `public/rarity-banners/` (replacing the old mismatched files 1:1, same five filenames). Two stray leftover files in that same folder (`common2.png`, `common3.png`, unreferenced by any code) were removed as part of the same pass since they'd otherwise sit there looking like unused art from this exact swap.
+
+**Scope: every REAL-rarity call site, not the two special-purpose frames.** Reverted: `SlotCard`/`StashCard`/`ArmourStashCard` (gear), `ConsumableInfoCard` and the equipped-consumable card (potions), `EquipmentShopCard`/`ConsumableShopCard` (Vendor stock), and `RecipeScrollCard` (added after 0338 on the then-standard `rarity-frame-card` pattern, patch 0357 -- pulled into this revert too since it's a real-rarity card same as the rest, even though it predates none of the original Design A approval). NOT reverted, on purpose: `CurioCard`'s grey frame and `SlotCard`'s empty-slot silver outline -- neither is a real rarity (Curios have no rarity to key a banner lookup on; an empty slot has no item to show one for either), no replacement art was supplied for either, and nothing about the direct feedback was about those two. Both stay exactly as Design A left them, still driven by `CURIO_FRAME`/`EMPTY_SLOT_FRAME` and `.rarity-frame-card`/`.rarity-frame-card-outline` in app.css, completely untouched by this patch.
+
+**Implementation shape.** Every reverted call site drops the `rarity-frame-card` class and its inline `RARITY_FRAME[def.rarity]` background, and gets a `<div className="rarity-banner" style={{ backgroundImage: url(RARITY_BANNER[def.rarity]) }} />` inserted as the first child instead -- the exact same `.rarity-banner` CSS (`app.css`) that already existed, untouched, this whole time (it never stopped powering every item's detail MODAL -- `.modal-banner` is a distinct class, this is the actual `.rarity-banner` class that simply had no card callers left after 0338). No CSS changes were needed to bring it back: `position: absolute; inset: 0; background-size: contain; opacity: 0.42` already does the right thing against the new evenly-sized art, and `.item-card-summary`/`.rarity-banner-content`'s existing `position: relative; z-index: 1` already re-establishes the real content on top of it. The `rarity-card` marker class (patch 0322's padding bump) is preserved wherever it was already present, so pill/durability-bar spacing is unaffected.
+
+`RARITY_FRAME` (the per-rarity map in `util.ts`) has no remaining callers as of this patch -- left in place rather than deleted, in case a rarity-keyed frame is wanted again later, but flagged in this file's Cleanup items below for the next dead-code pass to reconsider.
+
+**Icon size, direct follow-up in the same request.** Every reverted card's `ItemIcon`/`ConsumableIcon`/`RecipeIcon` now passes `size={48}` explicitly (up from IconBox's own 40px default) -- a modest bump asked for directly ("scale it up a little bit to fit nicely"), not a redesign; the two Vendor shop cards already used `size={41}` under the old system and were left as-is rather than bumped again. Worth a live look once this lands -- open to a follow-up nudge either direction on the exact icon scale.
+
+**Verified.** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build` both pass clean against every touched file, and the two now-unused `RARITY_FRAME` imports (`EquipmentPanel.tsx`/`VendorsPanel.tsx`) were removed rather than left dangling. Not re-screenshotted against a live render this round -- no headless Chromium available in this session's sandbox to confirm visually the way patches 0338-0342 were able to. Worth a real look in-game before considering this fully closed, especially the new icon scale on a busy StashCard (icon + name + several pills + durability bar all sharing the same banner).
+
